<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2403" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ămyntas</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμύντας</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The father of the Macedonian king Philip</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep. Reg.
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 7, 4</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ămyntĭă-dēs</span></b> ,
				ae, m.
			<i>patr.</i>, <i>a descendant of
			Amyntas</i>, i. e. <i>Philip</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
			297</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Name of a shepherd</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 3,
				66</span></i>.</div>
